Dang it, Bob, you just undid your bit of good! =A0You have again saddled BP=
FK with the paradoxical task of now documenting a language that ceased to e=
xist in 1997 (if even then). =A0You had said its task was to work out how t=
he presumably inadequate descriptions had been filled out, a reasonable tas=
k. =A0But that would not be a description of CLL Lojban =A0but of what that=
 has become. =A0I suppose that a compromise approach would be to find out f=
or each piece when it was possible to give an adequate account and to give =
that account and close that piece, ignoring what came after (except, perhap=
s, to note if a more complete account became available and then use that). =
=A0Or (ultimately a more useful thing) to trace all the developments, take =
the first adequate one as the baseline and the rest as the first proposals =
for revision. =A0In no case would this be, except accidentally, CLL Lojban =
(nor, if BPFK has any job to do, would one expect it to be). =A0
The sensible approach (and what I think was actually intended -- certainly =
after it became clear that the baselining was not going to be done in a sho=
rt time) is to close a corpus (we do have a good searchable corpus somewher=
e, don't we) at some date certain (tomorrow, say or June 1, 2014 anyhow) an=
d describe that language synchronically and diachronically, then take the s=
ynchronic as a baseline with notes on how it evolved from CLL based on the =
diachronic data. =A0This is a nice simple field linguist job, made consider=
ably easier by all the tools in CLL and since. =A0All it needs is warm bodi=
es with computers, since very little serious thought is required.




On Friday, May 23, 2014 9:33 PM, "Bob LeChevalier, President and Founder - =
LLG" <lojbab@lojban.org> wrote:
=20


On 5/22/2014 6:26 PM, v4hn wrote:
> I see why you consider irregular gismu "more practical" than completing t=
he byfy.
> Yet, I politely disagree when you say that finishing
> http://www.lojban.org/tiki/BPFK+Section%3A+Contact+Spatial
> and
> http://www.lojban.org/tiki/BPFK+Section%3A+Termsets
> is not practical at all and tries to define a 10-year old language.

Let me correct this.=A0 The purpose of the BPFK is to document the 17 year=
=20
old language (i.e that of 1997 when CLL was written) as a basis for=20
MODIFYING That baseline to reflect the current language.

lojbab

